+## 1. Guarded standard-bore canonicalization
+
+- [ ] 1.1 Extend the pure retrieval canonicalization boundary to emit at most one distinct additive representation containing catalog-native standard-bore vocabulary only for supported ball-valve queries with explicit standard-execution or standard-passage wording; verify focused unit tests assert exact source and alternate query text for representative Russian phrase variants.
+- [ ] 1.2 Preserve all source requirements in the alternate and block the new expansion for generic standard wording, other product families, unsupported/no-product text, and explicit full- or reduced-bore wording; verify focused no-op and conflicting-requirement tests.
+
+## 2. Additive-path regression coverage
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Verify the existing hybrid retrieval path issues both original and standard-bore alternate queries only when the alternate is distinct, deduplicates candidate IDs, and retains original-query candidates after alternate-query retrieval failure; add or update mocked hybrid-retriever tests.
+- [ ] 2.2 Verify hybrid matcher integration preserves the original normalized tender string as reranker input, `MatchResult.query`, and serialized output for an eligible standard-execution query; add or update a recording-retriever/mocked-reranker test.
+
+## 3. Local verification
+
+- [ ] 3.1 Run focused query-canonicalization, hybrid-retriever, and matcher tests, then run `python -m pytest -q`; resolve any product-code test failures without changing prompts, final-selection logic, catalog data, or index configuration.

